import BaseLayout from '../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
---
<BaseLayout title="Privacy — PARADOX" description="How PARADOX handles authentication, saved agents, scan history, analytics and GitHub API usage." canonical="https://paradox.engineer/privacy/">
  <main class="legal">
    <p class="label">PRIVACY</p>
    <h1>What we store, and what we don't.</h1>
    <article>
      <p>You can search, browse and run static analysis without an account. Authentication is optional and used for saved agents and scan history.</p>
      <h2>Authentication</h2>
      <p>When configured, accounts are handled by Supabase Auth (email/password and optional GitHub OAuth). Email verification and password reset are provided by that service.</p>
      <h2>Saved agents and scan history</h2>
      <p>If you sign in, PARADOX stores the repository URL, name, verdict, scores and a small JSON summary of detections — not full repository source — under your user id with row-level security.</p>
      <h2>Analytics</h2>
      <p>Google Analytics 4 records product events such as search, verify, save and signup. Passwords, tokens, API keys and private repository contents are not intended to be sent as event parameters.</p>
      <h2>Cookies</h2>
      <p>GA4 and, on some legacy pages, advertising scripts may set cookies according to those providers. PARADOX session cookies come from Supabase when auth is enabled.</p>
      <h2>GitHub API</h2>
      <p>Verification requests public GitHub metadata and file contents. GitHub sees the requester IP (browser) or the Edge Function IP (when deployed). Do not submit private repositories.</p>
      <h2>Retention</h2>
      <p>Browser analysis cache is local and short-lived. Server-side summaries, when enabled, should expire or be overwritten when HEAD changes. Delete saved rows and history from the dashboard.</p>
      <h2>Contact</h2>
      <p>Privacy questions: <a href="mailto:pradhumansingh196@gmail.com">pradhumansingh196@gmail.com</a>.</p>
    </article>
  </main>
</BaseLayout>
